  "content": "## Account and money\n\nBefore investigating a payment or moving money, confirm the account and mode\nwith `get_stripe_account_info`. A Connect account's objects belong to that\naccount, rather than the platform's account. Sandbox objects do not establish anything about live\ncustomers, revenue or payouts.\n\nResolve ids before acting. Stripe ids identify types: `cus_` customer, `sub_`\nsubscription, `ch_` charge, `pi_` PaymentIntent, `in_` invoice and `acct_`\naccount. A plausible-looking id can refer to a different object or to nobody.\n\nAmounts are integers in the currency's minor unit: 1099 is 10.99 USD, while\n10 is 10 JPY. Keep currencies separate when totaling balances or payments.\n\n## Payment investigations\n\nA PaymentIntent's `latest_charge` joins it to the charge holding the payment's\n`outcome`, `failure_code` and `failure_message`. Follow that reference to\nexplain a decline. Search supports a documented field set for each resource;\ncharge search has no `payment_intent` field. Resolve the parent and follow its\nreference when the needed relationship is not searchable.\n\nSearch is eventually consistent; use a direct object read to reconcile a\nrecent write. A POST's idempotency key identifies the exact operation and\nparameters. Stripe v1 may prune keys after 24 hours, so reconcile the object\nbefore attempting the operation outside that window. A new key can create a\nsecond payment or refund.\n\nIn v1 requests, an empty string (`\"\"`) or `null` unsets a field.\n\n## Data reduction and boundaries\n\nKeep only the customer and payment facts the question needs. Reduce lists to\ncounts, totals or matching records before returning them to the conversation.\nUse the account and balance summaries when their projections answer the task;\nother account fields and balance transactions are available through the API.\n\nCredential creation, customer/account sign-in links, secret payload expansions,\nfull Issuing card details, file uploads and the meter-event stream are outside\nthis connection's surface. Use the Dashboard or application server for those\nflows. Single meter events remain available. A guest Checkout payment page is\navailable only when it is unbound to a Customer or Account and cannot manage\nsaved payment methods; use a payment link or hosted invoice for other cases.\n\n## Conventions\n\n- **Paging:** while `page.hasMore` is true, continue with `page.nextCursor` unchanged. For `stripe_api_details`, `stripe_api_read`, `stripe_api_search`, pass it as the top-level `cursor`; omit raw paging anchors on continuations. Keep the original method, path, filters, page size, fields and headers. The last page has no `nextCursor`. If `page.hasMore` is true without a cursor, the data is incomplete and continuation was withheld. When approaching execute_code's per-program call limit, return page.nextCursor before the call that would exceed it and continue in the next program; don't restart.\n- **Results:** `fields` narrows a read's result to the dot paths you name. `truncated` lists the dot paths a result cut for size; the ids that fetch what was cut stay in the result.\n- **Hatch:** `stripe_api_search` finds this API's operations and reads no account data, `stripe_api_details` shows one operation's contract, and `stripe_api_read` calls a reviewed read. `stripe_api_write` calls a reviewed write; the host may ask the user to confirm it. An operation without a reviewed verdict is refused. 15 operations are refused by design; use `stripe_api_details` with the method and path to inspect an operation's contract and refusal.\n- **Writes:** a write is sent once and never retried. When its outcome is unknown, read the target before repeating it. A write that takes `idempotencyKey` may be repeated with the same key and arguments while the vendor retains it.\n- **Errors:** codes come from the vendor's statuses and error facts, never its prose. `not_found` means the record does not exist; this API tells absence from a permission gap. `conflict` means: HTTP 409 when the request conflicts with another request, including a concurrent use of the same idempotency key; HTTP 429 with code lock_timeout when another request holds the object's lock.\n- **Withheld values:** a value withheld for safety reads `\"[redacted]\"`. Writes refuse whole marker values and withheld links; longer prose may mention the marker. Paths and queries refuse any containment.",
